    "text": "The radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> of a nucleus of mass number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> can be estimated by the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. It follows that the mass density of n nucleus is of the order of: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#8773;</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>neut&#160;</mtext></msub><mo>&#8771;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
